1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,359
Chapter-12. 
Ethan Bruce POV

2
00:00:02,359 --> 00:00:07,200
I sat in the security room until the blue glare of the monitors seared into my retinas.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,284
The loop played over and over.

4
00:00:09,284 --> 00:00:11,304
The door opening.The jump.The roll.

5
00:00:11,304 --> 00:00:13,425
The gray sedan speeding into the night.

6
00:00:13,425 --> 00:00:14,460
She was gone.

7
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:17,602
The silence in the house wasn't peaceful; it was oppressive.

8
00:00:17,602 --> 00:00:21,409
It pressed against my eardrums like deep water, threatening to crush me.

9
00:00:21,409 --> 00:00:26,754
I stood up.My legs felt stiff, heavy as lead, like I had aged twenty years in twenty minutes.

10
00:00:26,754 --> 00:00:31,163
I needed to see it.I needed to see the physical proof that she hadn't just left for the night.

11
00:00:31,163 --> 00:00:33,618
I needed to see the void she left behind.

12
00:00:33,618 --> 00:00:36,416
I forced myself down the hallway to the east wing.

13
00:00:36,416 --> 00:00:39,062
This was her sanctuary.Her art studio.

14
00:00:39,062 --> 00:00:44,102
The only room in the estate where Ilene wasn't allowed-the only place that was truly Aurora's.

15
00:00:44,102 --> 00:00:45,454
I pushed the door open.

16
00:00:45,454 --> 00:00:49,042
I expected the earthy smell of turpentine and oil paint.

17
00:00:49,042 --> 00:00:57,622
I expected the chaos of canvases stacked against the walls, the splatter of color on the floor that she refused to clean because she said it was part of the process.

18
00:00:57,622 --> 00:01:00,737
Instead, I was met with the chemical sting of bleach.

19
00:01:00,737 --> 00:01:01,785
The room was white.

20
00:01:01,785 --> 00:01:03,852
Stark, blinding, clinical white.

21
00:01:03,852 --> 00:01:05,337
The canvases were gone.

22
00:01:05,337 --> 00:01:08,871
The easels were dismantled and stacked in the corner like firewood.

23
00:01:08,871 --> 00:01:10,660
The floor had been scrubbed raw.

24
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:11,896
There was nothing here.

25
00:01:11,896 --> 00:01:14,007
It looked like a room waiting for a tenant.

26
00:01:14,007 --> 00:01:17,992
Not a room where my wife had spent five years pouring her soul onto fabric.

27
00:01:17,992 --> 00:01:19,875
She hadn't just left, Ethan.

28
00:01:19,875 --> 00:01:21,239
She had erased herself.

29
00:01:21,239 --> 00:01:22,979
I walked to the center of the room.

30
00:01:22,979 --> 00:01:26,560
My footsteps echoed, sharp and lonely against the bare walls.

31
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:27,778
She had planned this.

32
00:01:27,778 --> 00:01:30,472
You don't exorcise a room like this in an hour.

33
00:01:30,472 --> 00:01:35,409
She had been packing, scrubbing, and erasing while I was busy holding Ilene's hand.

34
00:01:35,409 --> 00:01:37,718
A soft scuffle behind me made me turn.

35
00:01:37,718 --> 00:01:39,894
It was Maria, the head housekeeper.

36
00:01:39,894 --> 00:01:44,601
She stood in the doorway, twisting her apron in her hands until her knuckles turned white.

37
00:01:44,601 --> 00:01:46,416
Her eyes were red and swollen.

38
00:01:46,416 --> 00:01:48,103
"Mr. Bruce," she whispered.

39
00:01:48,103 --> 00:01:49,306
"Where is it?" I asked.

40
00:01:49,306 --> 00:01:52,877
My voice sounded like gravel grinding together."Where is her art?"

41
00:01:52,877 --> 00:01:54,102
"She burned it, Sir."

42
00:01:54,102 --> 00:01:55,403
I froze."What?"

43
00:01:55,403 --> 00:01:58,633
"Two days ago.In the incinerator out back.She said..."

44
00:01:58,633 --> 00:02:00,172
Maria choked on a sob.

45
00:02:00,172 --> 00:02:02,695
"She said that trash doesn't belong in a palace."

46
00:02:02,695 --> 00:02:04,006
My chest constricted.

47
00:02:04,006 --> 00:02:07,152
That was something Ilene had said to her at dinner last week.

48
00:02:07,152 --> 00:02:08,501
"Why didn't you stop her?"

49
00:02:08,501 --> 00:02:10,949
I snapped, the anger flaring hot and fast.

50
00:02:10,949 --> 00:02:13,221
"I tried.She told me it was an order."

51
00:02:13,221 --> 00:02:18,378
Maria looked up at me, and for the first time in ten years, I saw open judgment in her eyes.

52
00:02:18,378 --> 00:02:22,200
"She came back from the Gala tonight, Sir. She came back to get her bag."

53
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,082
"You saw her?"

54
00:02:23,082 --> 00:02:24,512
"Yes.She was crying.

55
00:02:24,512 --> 00:02:25,987
She didn't have her crutches.

56
00:02:25,987 --> 00:02:28,735
She was limping so bad I thought she would fall."

57
00:02:28,735 --> 00:02:30,020
"Why didn't you call me?"

58
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:34,061
"I tried to help her," Maria said, her voice gaining a sudden, sharp edge.

59
00:02:34,061 --> 00:02:35,599
"I asked her to wait for you.

60
00:02:35,599 --> 00:02:36,990
I told her you would fix it."

61
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:39,349
I took a threatening step toward her."And?"

62
00:02:39,349 --> 00:02:42,497
"She laughed, Sir.It was a terrible, broken sound.

63
00:02:42,497 --> 00:02:44,333
She said there was nothing to fix.

64
00:02:44,333 --> 00:02:45,691
She said she saw you."

65
00:02:45,691 --> 00:02:46,571
I stopped dead.

66
00:02:46,571 --> 00:02:47,627
"Saw me what?"

67
00:02:47,627 --> 00:02:49,564
"She said she saw you kiss Miss Wolf.

68
00:02:49,564 --> 00:02:50,943
She said you looked happy."

69
00:02:50,943 --> 00:02:53,579
The air left my lungs as if I'd been gutted.

70
00:02:53,579 --> 00:02:55,804
I didn't kiss Ilene because I wanted to.

71
00:02:55,804 --> 00:02:58,369
I kissed her to shut her up.To stop the scene.

72
00:02:58,369 --> 00:03:03,171
To protect the Family's image in front of the Commission.It was a tactic.A strategy.

73
00:03:03,171 --> 00:03:05,169
But Aurora didn't see a strategy.

74
00:03:05,169 --> 00:03:07,511
She saw her husband choosing his mistress.

75
00:03:07,511 --> 00:03:08,792
"Get out," I whispered.

76
00:03:08,792 --> 00:03:11,997
Maria didn't move."She left her wedding ring, Mr. Bruce.

77
00:03:11,997 --> 00:03:14,337
She said it was too heavy to carry anymore."

78
00:03:14,337 --> 00:03:15,727
"Get out!" I roared.

79
00:03:15,727 --> 00:03:20,664
Maria flinched and hurried away, leaving the echo of my shout to bounce off the empty walls.

80
00:03:20,664 --> 00:03:22,758
I was alone in the white room.

81
00:03:22,758 --> 00:03:24,407
I looked at the sterile walls.

82
00:03:24,407 --> 00:03:26,432
I had built a fortress to keep her safe.

83
00:03:26,432 --> 00:03:28,800
I had killed men who looked at her wrong.

84
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,114
I was the Underboss.

85
00:03:30,114 --> 00:03:32,987
I was the monster in the dark who protected the innocent.

86
00:03:32,987 --> 00:03:37,147
But standing in the bleach-scented void of her studio, I realized the truth.

87
00:03:37,147 --> 00:03:38,488
I wasn't the protector.

88
00:03:38,488 --> 00:03:40,584
I was the reason she needed protection.
